**How to implement.** Opening a kit resolves its library snapshot first, in the one import dialog when a row needs a decision (001 §E 'Resolution on open … One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md §10.1 'The import dialog opens … on a kit whose snapshot needs decisions'; §10.3 identify → confirm; step 141's doc: a kit whose rows all reuse MUST still show every row before confirmation; step 144: `ResolveKitSnapshot`). (1) In `Program.fs`' `LauncherWindow`, step 154's local function, on `Ok opened`: when `opened.pendingDecisions` (step 150) is empty the window opens as before. Otherwise it opens `ImportDialogWindow(context.catalogueImports, ResolveKitSnapshot (opened.library, opened.decisions), onApplied)` (steps 108, 144) and no constructor window yet. `onApplied applied` calls `opened.withRebindings applied.outcome.rebindings` (step 150): `Ok resolved` opens the constructor window over `resolved` in the asked mode; `Error e` closes the kit and shows `launcherKitErrorText` with `e.describe`. When the dialog closes without an Apply (its `Closed` with no `onApplied` before it, tracked by one local flag at this IO edge), the kit is closed (`close`, step 131) and nothing opens, so a cancelled resolution leaves the kit unlocked and the library unchanged. A read-only open (step 155) resolves the same way, because resolution writes nothing to the kit (step 141). No message or id is added. (2) Tests, in `LauncherTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`; the kits are written through `openKitAt`, `writeSnapshot` (step 138) and `close`. `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`: over a kit whose `library/` holds the snapshot of a test-local user material the app's library does not hold, clicking Main opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` and no constructor window; pressing its `importApplyButton`, the rows on their defaults (keep the kit's copy), opens one `MainConstructorWindow`, and the app's library still does not hold the material (`context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryHeldEntry` answers `None`). `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`: over the same kind of kit, pressing `importCancelButton` opens no constructor window and leaves no `.oc/lock`. `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`: over a kit holding only Silicon's Built-in snapshot, clicking Main MUST open one ImportDialogWindow displaying the Reuse row and no constructor. Cancel MUST release the kit without library writes; opening again and pressing Apply MUST open one MainConstructorWindow with database entries and the import log unchanged. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher keeps its code. After this step `git grep -n -E "SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy" -- Berreman/` still finds nothing. The declared opener acceptance fact MUST include an all-Reuse snapshot: every row MUST be visible; no constructor MUST open before Apply; Cancel MUST close the pending kit without changing database entries or log; applying defaults MUST open with no database writes. An empty snapshot list alone MAY bypass the dialog.

**Acceptance.** After resolution on open lands, a picked kit whose snapshot has a row that is not `SameContentHash` MUST open the import dialog before the constructor, Apply MUST open the constructor over the resolved overlay and Cancel MUST open nothing and release the kit, and `git grep -n -E "SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`, `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
